    // the wrapper's larger retirement.
    dissolution: bound_dissolution(ref: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.serving.srv1_serving_launch", decl_name: "srv1_serving_api_key_substitution_node")),
  ),
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.serving.srv1_serving_launch", decl_name: "srv1_serving_wrapper"),
    reason: "THE DEVICE FLAG THE WRAPPER PASSES. The launch's device selection is the declared GPU group srv1_serving_gpu_group; the installed wrapper's `--device` is CONSTRUCTED from it via srv1_serving_docker_device_flag (one home for the UUID: gunbc.fleet.gpu_device_observation, admitted through gunbc.fleet.gpu_power_state_policy, rendered by srv1_serving_docker_device_words) and interpolated into srv1_serving_wrapper.body — so the `nvidia.com/gpu=all` wildcard is UNWRITABLE rather than validated away, and srv1_serving_device_gate refuses the deploy install unless the group resolves to a fully admitted set (a pending member or a TP=2 declaration missing a member keeps the one-card config running and refuses the widening; DESIGN 5: refuse, never widen). The retained wrapper IS the script the boot unit installs for the next boot (gunbc.live_deploy.srv1_serving_engine_unit srv1_serving_engine_wrapper_text), so its single authority is the MODEL. What this row still owes is the RUNTIME half: the RUNNING container was launched from the pre-change `all` wrapper (gunbc.host.srv1_serving_startup_receipt wrapper_sha256_hex), so the installed model body is ahead of the host — srv1_serving_wrapper_adoption types that divergence PendingOperatorRelaunch. Relaunching srv1's engine to adopt it is operator maintenance this module never performs (the boot unit installs the wrapper and never starts it; gunbc.recurring_failure_mode a_relaunch_from_the_retained_wrapper_reverts_an_image_applied_outside_it). The row closes when a startup receipt reads the running wrapper's sha equal to the installed body's, which fires srv1_serving_device_flag_adoption_node.",
